Z||000000||LivoniaFieroGT||06-04-2001||07:48 AM||||If installing a V8 into one my Fieros.  Choice of 4 speed or auto.  I've heard the 4 speed is good to some level of power before breaking... don't know the point but what of the automatic.  can a standard unaltered auto handle a strong V8?  What alterations are possible to endure the power?<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||06-04-2001||08:44 AM||||It all depends on how you drive. Archie has put V8's with the 5sp Isuzu and the auto's. I have a 275 Hp 3800 with the 5sp Getrag and 50,000 miles so far no prob. You can break any tranny if you try. ( you could have seen both set-ups - Archie and me - at the Power Tour in Pontiac last May)<P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_1.gif">  <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||06-04-2001||11:44 AM||||You'll want to use as new of an automatic as the motor will support. I.E. Use a 90-91 TH125 if you stay 3 speed... Early TH125's have known weaknesses that probably won't take as much abuse as the later ones. TH125 and it's 4 speed relatives were modified and upgraded thru the whole life of the product so the newer the better. Even then you'll likely want to do a full rebuild and maybe a new chain before putting it in the car.||||reg||1
Z||000003||LivoniaFieroGT||06-04-2001||11:09 PM||||What is involved in a 350 with a 4 speed trans as an install?  How do I come up an axle combo that will fit?  Is this a bad and too expensive idea?||||reg||1
